  @test/operations/runtest-zero_out_local_decl-extension

== tests compiling or executing kernel text they built themselves ==
They pin nothing, and a codegen change breaks them all the same (gh-ocannl-1685): a staged
callback's text is emitted verbatim and renamed by nothing, a [?prelowered] lowering is an IR
shape the pipeline never emits, a shipped kernel compiled alone loses the batch around it. Run
them on every GPU backend. The rules are stated in test/support/kernel_exec_scan.ml.
support values reaching such text, derived from the sources:
Bench_harness.compile_shipped_kernel [prelowered compile]
Bench_harness.dominant_kernel [through Bench_harness.time_shipped_kernels]
Bench_harness.measure_and_emit [through Bench_harness.dominant_kernel]
Bench_harness.run_self_test [through Bench_harness.dominant_kernel; through Bench_harness.measure_and_emit]
Bench_harness.time_shipped_kernels [through Bench_harness.compile_shipped_kernel]
Bench_harness.time_shipped_segments [through Bench_harness.time_shipped_kernels]
Ll_test.execute [through Ll_test.execute_with_census]
Ll_test.execute_with_census [through Ll_test.run_routine]
Ll_test.link [prelowered compile]
Ll_test.link_finalized [through Ll_test.link]
Ll_test.optimize_and_execute [through Ll_test.execute]
Ll_test.run [through Ll_test.run_routine]
Ll_test.run_routine [through Ll_test.link]

